COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from AK292211.1, AK222748.1,
            X75308.1 and CA413743.1.
            This sequence is a reference standard in the RefSeqGene project.
            
            On Nov 23, 2018 this sequence version replaced NM_002427.3.
            
            Summary: This gene encodes a member of the peptidase M10 family of
            matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs). Proteins in this family are
            involved in the breakdown of extracellular matrix in normal
            physiological processes, such as embryonic development,
            reproduction, and tissue remodeling, as well as in disease
            processes, such as arthritis and metastasis. The encoded
            preproprotein is proteolytically processed to generate the mature
            protease. This protease cleaves type II collagen more efficiently
            than types I and III. It may be involved in articular cartilage
            turnover and cartilage pathophysiology associated with
            osteoarthritis. Mutations in this gene are associated with
            metaphyseal anadysplasia. This gene is part of a cluster of MMP
            genes on chromosome 11. [provided by RefSeq, Jan 2016].
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
